  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.406,
            0.071,
            0.813,
            0.089
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "How Quantities Combine: Understanding Data"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.863,
            0.071,
            0.881,
            0.086
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.11,
            0.882,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Method 1 does not work because it treats the average heights of seniors and of juniors equally — but there are many more seniors than juniors!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.12,
            0.156,
            0.379,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.12,
                0.156,
                0.379,
                0.346
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_1_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.443,
            0.152,
            0.822,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Shreyas calculated it differently as"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.467,
            0.183,
            0.73,
            0.222
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{(165.5 \\times 8) + (149.33 \\times 3)}{8 + 3}"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.468,
            0.247,
            0.705,
            0.317
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_6.jpg",
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}=\\frac{1324 + 448}{11} &= \\frac{1772}{11} \\\\&= 161.09.\\end{aligned}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.443,
            0.327,
            0.876,
            0.348
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you understand why this also works?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.352,
            0.881,
            0.391
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can you see why "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "1 6 5 . 5 \\times 8"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " gives the sum of the heights of all the seniors and 149.33 × 3 gives the sum of the heights of all the juniors?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.392,
            0.881,
            0.432
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This phenomenon is explained below with a generalisation. Suppose we have two collections of data — Collection 1 and Collection 2."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.446,
            0.486,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose the data in Collection 1, having n values, is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "X_{1},X_{2},X_{3},\\ldots,X_{n}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The average of Collection 1 is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.508,
            0.446,
            0.883,
            0.489
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Suppose the data in Collection 2, having m values, is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y _ { 1 } , y _ { 2 } , y _ { 3 } , \\ldots , y _ { m }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.519,
            0.375,
            0.556
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_12.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{X_{_1} + X_{_2} + X_{_3} + \\cdots + X_{_n}}{n} = a."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.51,
            0.492,
            0.832,
            0.514
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The average of Collection 2 is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.511,
            0.521,
            0.768,
            0.56
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_14.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{y_{1}+y_{2}+y_{3}+\\cdots+y_{m}}{m}=b."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.564,
            0.488,
            0.605
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus the sum of the data in Collection 1 is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.509,
            0.567,
            0.811,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus the sum of the data in Collection 2 is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.121,
            0.611,
            0.388,
            0.633
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "X_{1} + X_{2} + X_{3} + \\cdots + X_{n} = an."
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.512,
            0.613,
            0.789,
            0.636
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_18.jpg",
          "content": "y_{1} + y_{2} + y_{3} + \\cdots + y_{m} = bm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.641,
            0.617,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The average of the combined data is therefore"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.669,
            0.868,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(Sum of values in Collection 1) + (Sum of values in Collection 2) (Number of values in Collection 1) + (Number of values in Collection 2)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.455,
            0.717,
            0.579,
            0.754
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_1_equation_21.jpg",
          "content": "\\operatorname { = } { \\frac { a n + b m } { n + m } } ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.774,
            0.535,
            0.909
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 2:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Jaspreet recently learnt cycling. She has explored different routes in her town. She tracked how much time she cycled on weekdays over the last 3 weeks. Find the mean time spent cycling per weekday over the last 3 weeks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
